            p("Kubernetes offers a simple form: each Service gets a stable DNS name, such as <code>payments.default.svc.cluster.local</code>, that leads to its current Pods [[k8s-dns]]. Watch DNS caching: a client that caches an answer too long keeps calling instances that are gone."),
            h("Traffic before it is ready"),
            p("A new instance that gets traffic before it has loaded its caches or connected to its database fails its first requests. A readiness probe tells Kubernetes when a container is ready to accept traffic, and Kubernetes stops sending traffic to containers that are not ready [[k8s-probes]]. Slow start then ramps up the share of traffic a new instance gets, instead of giving it a full share at once [[envoy-slow-start]]. On shutdown, stop taking new requests and let the ones in flight finish before exiting."),
            h("What if the registry goes down?"),
